# claude-account — project → account mapping
#
# One rule per line:   <account>   <path prefix>
# First match wins: write from the most specific to the most generic.
# '~' is expanded. <account> maps to ~/.claude-accounts/<account>, except for the
# reserved name 'default', which means ~/.claude.
#
# An account that does not exist yet is skipped and resolution continues, so a row
# written ahead of time breaks nothing.
#
# Examples:
# work      ~/projects/acme
# personal  ~/projects/side-projects
# default   ~/projects/acme/open-source     # subfolder that goes back to the default account
